      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Two model calls per memory",
      "items": [
        "One embedding call and one extraction call",
        "Loading the example persona batches all 14 into two calls",
        "Guardrails run before either, so a rejected request costs no quota"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Encrypted before it leaves",
      "items": [
        "Encryption lives in the store's payload serialisation",
        "No call site can write plaintext by forgetting to",
        "Graph entity labels stay readable \u2014 a documented tradeoff"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Extraction is best-effort",
      "items": [
        "A failed or unparseable extraction never fails the ingest",
        "Relationship types are sanitised before touching Cypher",
        "Dangling and self edges are dropped, not stored"
      ]
